Aerie-Purpose: Report a common screen size (the smallest of seven common sizes that fits the window) from window.screen, device-width and device-height, put the window at 0,0 and report 24-bit colour and one screen, so the real display is no fingerprint surface (issue #116).
Aerie-Upstream-Area: third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/screen.cc (Screen::GetRect, colorDepth, isExtended), third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/local_dom_window.cc (screenX, screenY), third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/media_values.cc (CalculateDeviceWidth, CalculateDeviceHeight), third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/screen_masking.h, third_party/blink/public/common/helium_noise/ (HeliumNoiseFeature::kScreen), content/browser/helium_noise/noise_token_data.cc, third_party/blink/common/features.cc (kHeliumNoiseScreen)
Aerie-Kind: hook

HeliumNoiseFeature::kScreen is a new surface token, added the way hardening/0010 adds kWebGL: a
session token in HeliumNoiseTokenData that GetTokens derives per site, and a renderer that receives
it only when protection is on for the site. "Token present" therefore means "protected here", and
the global switch and the per-site switch give the real values back without a renderer change. The new
feature kHeliumNoiseScreen (on by default) switches the surface off for the Bench's negative control.

A protected window reports the smallest of 1280x800, 1366x768, 1440x900, 1680x1050, 1920x1080,
2560x1440 and 3840x2160 that is at least as wide and as tall as the window's outer size (a window
larger than the last one keeps its own size, so the screen is never smaller than the window).
availWidth/availHeight equal the screen size, availLeft/availTop and screenX/screenY are 0,
colorDepth and pixelDepth are 24 and isExtended is false. The device-width and device-height media
features read the same value, so matchMedia agrees with screen.width. outerWidth, outerHeight and
devicePixelRatio are not changed: the outer size is the inner size plus the real browser chrome
already, and a false pixel ratio breaks image selection and canvas sizing. There is no letterboxing.

The bucket list, the choice and the decision (ShouldProtectScreen) are pure code with unit tests in
overlay/components/aerie_screen. One Blink helper, screen_masking.h in core/frame, reads the feature
switches, the token and the window rectangle (the one outerWidth reads, so it needs no layout and is
safe during style recalculation). Full screen is not touched: it sizes the page from the real
display on the browser side.

Workers have no screen. A frame of another site in the same window reads its own site's token.

